WEBVTT

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.960
All right.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.770
But...

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:14.550
there really is something surprising 
about your growth, Elmo.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.070
Really?

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.070
Of course.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.150
You acquired the language rather quickly,

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.110
and considerable knowledge, as well.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.040
It's because the books in your 
room are interesting, Jolly.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.300
The books on alchemy were difficult, though.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.340
I see.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.360
You're very bright, Elmo.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:41.560
<i>But...</i>

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.750
<i>it's better that I have more insurance.</i>

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.370
Hey,

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.980
I have a request.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.700
What is it?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.680
Um,

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.900
I want to go out into the 
city with you, Jolly.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.370
Is that too much?

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:07.040
That's...

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.010
Jolly!

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.480
What?

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.240
Jolly was out walking with a child?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:54.860
Yes.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.860
It must have been someone else.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.860
I don't think so.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.630
I'm pretty positive I saw him.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.080
He looked happy and was smiling.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.300
Inconceivable!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.590
He's not one to dote on children.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.980
I would prefer that you

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:18.090
stay away from him in general.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.000
You said that the other day, too.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.200
I will pour tea into this 
cup and add honey to it.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.690
The substance in the tea,

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.710
called tannin, that gives tea its color,

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:43.840
interacts with the honey's iron content,

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.700
making it change color.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.640
Jolly drew this out of his research

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.310
and showed this to me as a child.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.500
As his student, I respect him for his

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.170
techniques and his research.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.090
However, his character is a 
completely different story.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.550
Luca...

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.030
My apologies, Milady.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.140
I've made you feel uncomfortable.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.800
However, in the past, Jolly...

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:20.190
No. One day, I will 
explain to you, Milady.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.950
It amazes me that you can eat 
lasagna so early in the morning.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.490
Why don't you eat 
something, too, Debito?

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:37.960
It'll cheer you up.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:40.020
No thanks.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.170
Are you okay?

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.300
At night, it's been hurting 
so much that I can't sleep.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.050
Even if I'm able to sleep,

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.810
all I see are unwanted nightmares.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:55.270
But...

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.390
I can't win against my sleepiness.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.420
I'm going home to sleep again.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.110
Maybe this time, 
I'll actually have a pleasant dream.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.450
Miss!

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.970
Princess!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.040
That's the kid from...

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.180
Apparently, he snuck into 
the mansion somehow.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:19.970
I couldn't just send him away,

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.290
so we've been playing.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.550
Right, Elmo?

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.170
Yeah. I was told I could 
play outside today.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm really happy to see you again.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.680
Me, too.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.030
We were worried about you 
after the Piccolino!

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.430
You disappeared so suddenly.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.920
Sorry.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.410
It's just that I didn't 
want to worry Jolly.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.530
Jolly?

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.680
By some chance, were you two walking—

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.980
There you are.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.890
Jolly!

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.380
It's just about time for you 
to read your books, Elmo.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:53.840
Okay.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.330
So you two do know each other.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.330
Actually, how do you two 
even know each other?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.830
Don't worry, he's not 
an illegitimate child.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:05.590
Oh, yes, perfect timing.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.160
If I may ask a favor, Milady?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.050
What?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.920
I'd like you to deliver this to Debito,

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:14.400
and ask him to come to my lab.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.890
He doesn't seem to listen 
when I ask him myself.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:22.020
As the head of the Sword, 
I'd like you to fix that.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.230
All right.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.710
I'll leave it to you.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.160
Now, let's go.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:28.940
Okay.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.460
See you again!

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.370
Apparently, it's bothering him again.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:40.780
There's the thing with his eye,

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:42.580
but more importantly, 
he says that he can't sleep.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.460
I see.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.810
I will try to make a medicine for him.

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.550
It may help him a little.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.340
That would be great, Luca.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:57.530
Even though it's probably better if 
Jolly takes a look at him...

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.270
I don't see that happening.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.240
Their dislike for one 
another is rather deep.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.320
Though it isn't just Debito...

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:07.330
You're right.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:10.100
A lot has happened.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.950
If only there was something I could do.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.580
Your existence itself is plenty, Pace.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.960
Actually, the scary moon demon, Diavolo,

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.960
lives here on Regalo.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.290
It all happened one stormy night.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:40.600
An orphaned child came to this 
church in search of help.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.920
It was there, that the 
child met Diavolo.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.940
The child's soul was severed in two.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.530
One half became the demon's 
minion, Belzebù,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.570
who resides in the darkness, hiding.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.240
Even now, Diavolo's right eye

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.820
gleams in search of...

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.080
...his minion in this church.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.690
See? Right behind you.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.150
Bambina...

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:19.180
I heard your voice...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.400
I'm sorry for intruding.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.360
If it was anyone else, I'd kill them.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.200
However, you're more than 
welcome in here, Bambina.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.480
You came to have a siesta 
with me, didn't you?

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.080
N-No!

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.840
Bambina,

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.970
you should be glad that 
you're a signorina.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.780
Debito?

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.850
Don't look at me like that.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.500
Tell the old man,

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.150
that my right eye is doing fine.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:16.160
So much so, that I'd like to kill him.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:22.660
Go.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.130
That was really interesting.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:43.180
Well...

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.200
You're rather unexpected company.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.390
Do you have a minute?

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.030
I'm torturing Debito?

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.440
That's a rather harsh accusation.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:02.820
I've only been researching 
all of your Arcana powers.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.370
What you're doing may be for the family,

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.010
but I'd rather you stopped 
making people suffer.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.090
So, you understand.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:17.280
As you said, this is for the family.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.800
If it hasn't bothered you up to this point,

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.640
surely you can deal with it now.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:31.380
Pace.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.690
Oh, hey, Princess.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.160
Is Jolly in his room?

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.150
Yeah.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.350
What's wrong?

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.410
He asked me to do something 
pertaining to Debito.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:44.540
I see. Thanks for your hard work.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.650
Um, Pace...

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:57.120
Did something happen between 
Debito, Luca, and Jolly?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:08.140
You needn't worry about anything, Princess.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:19.000
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.350
It's about Jolly.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:24.910
Again?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.210
What do you mean, again?

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.150
You're always sticking your nose 
into other people's business.

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:32.440
Wanting to know the 
truth about everything

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:33.990
isn't always the right solution.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.470
Yes, but,

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:40.140
it was you who told me that I 
should be more aware of myself.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.050
What?

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.260
As Papa's daughter,

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.490
I'd like to know more about everyone.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.560
And I'd like to get along 
with everyone, if possible.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.190
You're asking for too much.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.400
What?

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.520
I also think there's something 
suspicious about Jolly.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:00.190
The suspicion of money laundering, 
my parents' medical files...

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.000
You can't approach him 
using normal methods.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.870
However, you do have a point.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.580
So, what do you want to do, specifically?

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.550
Is there something we can all do?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:18.210
I think it'd be a good opportunity.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.050
Well...

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.250
Oh, there you are!

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.950
I've been looking for you guys!

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.470
What is it?

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:31.610
Well, the priest asked if I'd help 
with cleaning the church.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.420
I won't be able to do it all myself,

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.180
so I figured I'd ask other family members.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.020
That's it, Fel!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.320
Yes.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:40.550
Huh?

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.000
<i>Isn't there something I can 
do for the two of them,</i>

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:49.970
<i>Mom?</i>

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.390
I'm curious if Jolly will come.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.930
Inviting him was all you could do.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.350
Now the rest is up to him.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.770
Let me help.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.480
Uh, h-hey...

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.600
C'mon, let's get a move on.

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:26.400
Yeah.

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.010
Those two...

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.490
He has to overcome his 
problems on his own.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:40.470
Did you hear anything 
about Libertá's past?

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:41.380
Nope.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.610
Nothing?

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:44.750
There's no need.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.340
It's none of my concern,

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.760
whether or not it's troubling him.

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:56.230
But it's apparent that he's 
trying to overcome something.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:04.500
Damn it.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.020
Cleaning the church first 
thing in the morning?

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.640
You've got to be kidding me.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.910
They always take care of 
us during the Piccolino.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.950
This is the least we can do.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:16.310
The Piccolino?

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.830
We're the ones that take care of it.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.420
We're only able to do it 
because this church is here.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:26.340
Being here brings back a lot of memories.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:31.730
Well, they're not all 
bad memories, are they?

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.430
I guess not.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:55.410
Don't hurt yourself, now.

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.770
Debito, Luca!

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.340
Come here a sec.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.120
Check this out.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.300
Wow, that's nostalgic.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.960
I can't believe it's still here.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:16.140
What's that?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.810
Pace, Luca, Debito.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:22.020
It's our initials that we 
carved into this years ago.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:26.230
At one time, we all lived 
in this church together.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:29.220
Along with Pace's mother.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.080
Well, those are good memories.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:36.200
Those were days filled 
with peace and innocence.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.410
We were all supposed to be cleaning 
the church, like we are today...

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.250
Debito, Pace. Where did you go?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.420
If we don't hurry and clean,

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.170
the priest will scold us.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:48.710
Shh!

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:51.900
Hey, you idiot!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:53.990
Found you.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:59.550
It took forever to finish cleaning,

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:02.600
because these two wouldn't stop playing.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.350
Well, we were kids.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.920
Yeah, we were kids.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:10.360
That's not an excuse, you two!

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.320
That sounds like a lot of fun.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.050
Do you want to play hide-and-seek 
for old time's sake?

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.370
Pace!

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.960
How about we play something 
much more interesting

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:22.170
than some kids' game, Bambina?

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.210
Debito!

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.140
We won't be playing hide-and-seek 
or any other game!

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.460
We came here to clean!

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:31.920
How disappointing.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:36.390
I was going to join in if you were 
going to play hide-and-seek.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.090
Jolly...

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:40.220
What the hell are you 
doing here, old man?

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:43.350
Now, that was uncalled for.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.980
I can't ignore Milady's request.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:52.060
Though, I did think it was 
an excellent opportunity

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:54.570
to check up on you since 
you wouldn't come to me.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.880
You shouldn't have come here.

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.830
Just seeing your face makes me sick.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.960
How dare you use us as tools?

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:08.790
You should strengthen your heart 
if you actually want to kill me.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.620
What?!

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:13.640
If I were to have Milady there

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.170
read your heart and point out

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:20.310
all of your darkness and weaknesses,

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:22.980
your Arcana powers 
would become stronger.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:26.940
Then you wouldn't have to rely

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.860
on the amethyst I implanted, 
in place of your right eye,

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.030
to control your Arcana powers.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:36.490
Jolly, please stop!

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:41.310
Don't you see that your words 
bring out others' animosity?

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.080
Well, well...

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:46.960
You're still worried about a mentor 
like me after all of this?

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:48.900
What a sweet child.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.160
You wanted to get along with everyone

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.760
in the family, did you not?

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.220
I'll let you in on a little secret.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:01.740
Luca, Debito, and Pace's stigmata

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.930
are the product of my experiments.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:06.060
What?

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:11.200
I experimented with many subjects

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.660
on how, exactly, 
the Tarocco chooses its host.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.220
These were the only three

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:18.500
who were able to establish contracts.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:22.670
I have no reason to be hated.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:26.160
The reason any of you strangers 
were able to stay in the family

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:29.580
is because I helped you establish 
contracts with the Tarocco.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:33.360
Especially you, you're able 
to control your powers

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.650
because of your right eye.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.260
You should be thanking me.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:47.300
I'll blow a hole in your head, 
right here and now.

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:50.430
How amusing.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:51.810
Do it.

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:55.860
But, can you actually defy me?

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.500
That's what I thought.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.920
There's no way that you 
could actually kill me.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.890
Stop this.

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:19.650
Papa and the family are behind 
all of your research.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:23.260
I've been holding back all 
this time with that in mind.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:26.960
Debito and Luca have been holding 
back even more than me.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:31.140
But if we hold back any longer,

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.790
our hearts are likely to turn black!

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.890
I can't sit idly by doing nothing

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:38.530
while my precious friends 
are being ridiculed!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:46.650
I told you to deal with it 
for the sake of the family.

00:19:46.650 --> 00:19:50.040
Debito and Luca will one day be 
able to settle their own fights.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:53.640
But our fight will be settled right now!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.300
Porci! Tutto trapassare!

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:15.520
Is that all you have to say, Pace?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:20.060
Doing this has changed nothing.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.780
Though you do have more to clean up now.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.130
What a beautiful friendship.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.100
Cheer up.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:40.630
You only had good intentions, Princess.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.940
Those guys and Jolly

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:45.340
would have butted heads sooner or later.

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.150
It's not your fault, Fel.

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:51.400
I wonder why Jolly conducted 
Tarocco experiments

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.850
on the three of them.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.020
I want to know why.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:01.030
Jolly is a member of the 
family that Papa chose.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.520
I don't think he's a bad person.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:07.610
Or you don't want to think 
of him as a bad person.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.560
You're too nice.

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:14.250
Well, that's what I like about you.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:18.260
Okay, Princess, let's stop moping!

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.460
Yes.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:36.470
What is that?

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:46.260
Elmo?

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.980
Curiosity killed the cat.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.620
He's an artificial human that I created.

00:21:57.270 --> 00:21:59.190
A homunculus.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.110
So you'll be able to find out

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:33.620
why I initiated the Arcana Duello

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.350
in the next episode?

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:36.770
Who cares about that?

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.040
More importantly, let's have a toast!

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:39.520
Salute!
